Lab 1: Setting Up the Environment
Objective
Install and configure essential open-source deep learning frameworks, developer tools, and containerization platforms locally to prepare your machine for hands-on labs.

Prerequisites
Start your Al Nafi-provided Ubuntu machine

Make sure your system is updated:

sudo apt update && sudo apt upgrade -y
Steps
Step 1: Set Up a Python Virtual Environment
Install python3-venv if not already available:

sudo apt install python3-venv -y
Create a virtual environment:

python3 -m venv dl-env
Activate the environment:

source dl-env/bin/activate
Step 2: Install Deep Learning Libraries
With your virtual environment activated:

Upgrade pip:

pip install --upgrade pip
Install TensorFlow, Keras, and PyTorch:

pip install tensorflow keras torch torchvision
Install Jupyter Notebook:

pip install notebook
Launch Jupyter Notebook to verify:

jupyter notebook
Press Ctrl+C to stop the notebook server after confirming it starts.

Step 3: Install Docker and Run a Container
Install Docker:

sudo apt install docker.io -y
Start and enable the Docker service:

sudo systemctl start docker
sudo systemctl enable docker
Run a simple container to verify:

sudo docker run hello-world
This confirms that Docker is working correctly.

Conclusion
In this lab, you successfully:

Set up a Python virtual environment for isolated development

Installed TensorFlow, Keras, PyTorch, and Jupyter Notebook for deep learning work

Installed Docker and verified it by running a container

You now have a fully functional local development environment ready for AI, ML, and DevOps experiments — all configured on your Al Nafi Ubuntu machine without needing cloud access.
